   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 20,
   "message": "An empty AZDO_REPO only prints a WARN and the run continues. The pod then clones, runs the whole agent session and only fails later in pr-azdo. Because the warning is a flag this is not a major, but the gap is cheap to close. Call `fail`/`finish` with a clear status before `run_agent` when AZDO_REPO cannot be derived, or at least record the warning on the work item, so the operator does not have to dig it out of pod logs. The ac7 WARN row should then assert that the run stops, not only that the message is printed.",
